# A1-P03 to A1-P06 — the Broken Mile, the First Edit, Why Oakhaven, First Sight.
# Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1313–1490.
# Scene: scenes/chapter1/path_to_oakhaven.tscn. A walk-and-talk: Data Vision
# unlocks through use, and Root Access through immediate danger, not
# curiosity.
# rhythm: clipped data_vision
# (The "Spirits? / No. / Runes? / No." exchange is a comic beat.)

# A1-P03: a tree flickers between healthy and burnt.
~ tree_flicker
set ch1_broken_mile_entered
Kaelen: Did you see that? The tree, just there.
Elara: Which part of it? The black or the green?
Kaelen: Both. It was burnt black, and then it wasn't. Like somebody flicked a switch.
Elara: Then I saw it. Mind the rut.
Kaelen: You're not even slowing down.
Elara: It happens. Not every day. Often enough that you stop pointing at it.
Kaelen: Burnt, then not burnt, nothing in between. Trees don't render like— trees don't do that.
Elara: These ones do. Keep walking. You can stare at trees once there's a wall behind you.

# Optional walk dialogue. It sets up the medium-term goal, Ironhold.
~ walk_manifest
Kaelen: If somebody else came out of that crater, where would they go?
Elara: East, to Oakhaven. Or south to Ironhold, if the south road's open. It mostly isn't.
Kaelen: What's Ironhold? Somewhere with people, I hope.
Elara: A city. Records, caravans, and a lot of people who enjoy making rules about records and caravans.
Kaelen: Rules about records. That was most of my job, before.
Elara: You say "before" like it's a place.
Kaelen: Never mind. I'm looking for a passenger manifest.
Elara: Say that in words a carter would know.
Kaelen: A list. The names of everyone who was on the plane with me.
Elara: Then Ironhold's where you'd ask. If anyone in this world keeps a list of names, it's them.
set ch1_ironhold_lead

# A collapsed cart blocks the road. Elara clears it with her corrupted arm.
~ cart
do elara_casts_cart
Kaelen (Internal): She's hiding a wince. She's had practice at it, and it still isn't enough.
? Kaelen (Internal): Do I say something, or let her have it?
- Your arm— => arm_ask
- (Say nothing.) => arm_silence

~ arm_ask
set elara_arm_noticed
Kaelen: Your arm—
Elara: —stays attached. Look at the road, not at me.
Kaelen: That spell hurt you. I saw your jaw go tight.
Elara: Did you want a prize, or just to be right?
Kaelen: Can I help? With the arm, I mean, not the cart.
Elara: With what, exactly? You've been here half a day.
Kaelen: ...I don't know yet. I'll tell you when I do.
Elara: Then don't promise me anything you haven't got.

~ arm_silence
set elara_arm_respected_silence
do trust elara 10
do elara_glances
# She notices that he noticed, and that he didn't say anything. No line.

# The next corrupted obstruction highlights a structural seam.
~ data_vision
set ch1_data_vision_unlocked
do unlock_data_vision
Kaelen: Hold on. There's something written over that, in the air.
Elara: Spirits?
Kaelen: No.
Elara: Runes?
Kaelen: No. It's— it looks like metadata.
Elara: "Metadata." The priests would love you. All those words, and not one of them moves a cart.
Kaelen: Labels, then. Everything here has labels on it: stability, owner, what it's for.
Elara: Everything has a name. We just don't write them on things.
Kaelen: Somebody did. Somebody sat down and wrote these on purpose.

# A1-P04 — The First Edit. A corrupted guardian blocks the only stable pass.
~ guardian_intro
Kaelen: Is there another way around it? A long way's fine. Any way's fine.
Elara: Not before dark. And I'm not taking you through Mosswood with the sky doing that.
do guardian_attacks

# Mid-fight, the guardian freezes for half a second.
~ guardian_directive
do show_directive
System: DIRECTIVE: DEFEND NEST.
System: TARGET FILTER: ALL.
System: ERROR: NEST_REFERENCE_NULL.
Kaelen: It's an if-statement. The nest's gone, and nobody told it.
Elara: A what? Stranger, it's coming back!
set root_access_unlocked
do root_access_open

# The player edited TARGET FILTER from ALL to FRACTURE_ENTITIES.
~ root_used
set ch1_root_first_edit
Elara: What did you just do?
Kaelen: Changed what it thinks it's defending against. Can I stop shaking before you ask how?
Elara: You reached inside a living thing and moved something around in it.
Kaelen: I think so? It's stopped swinging at us. I'm counting that as it working.
Elara: You do not say "I think so" after doing whatever that was.
do kaelen_hand_glitch
# His hand glitches for one frame. He notices. She notices. Neither says
# anything. Leave the silence.

# The player turned the aggression multiplier down instead of the filter.
~ root_used_calm
set ch1_root_first_edit
Elara: What did you just do?
Kaelen: Turned it down. Its anger, or whatever that number is. Down to something it can live with.
Elara: It's just standing there, staring at nothing. Like an old dog that's forgotten what it was barking at.
Kaelen: It's still guarding the nest. I just took out the part where it minds.
Elara: I'm not sure that's kinder than killing it.
do kaelen_hand_glitch

# The player won the fight without editing. Root stays discovered but unused.
~ root_refused
set ch1_root_discovered_unused
Kaelen (Internal): I could've changed it. The field was right there, waiting. I could've just...
Elara: You've got the face of someone adding up a thing they didn't do.
Kaelen: Still adding. Ask me again when I know whether I'm glad.

# A1-P05 — Why Oakhaven. A roadside rest above the village.
~ rest_stop
Elara: You keep taking that scrap out and looking at it. It hasn't changed.
Kaelen: There were a couple of hundred people on that plane. Maybe more. I never counted.
Elara: And you think they're here somewhere.
Kaelen: I think they're not in the crater. That's the whole list of things I actually know.
Elara: Not in the crater isn't the same as here.
Kaelen: I know. It's step one. I was hoping you had a step two.
Elara: Oakhaven first. Supper, a roof. Bran keeps the road ledger; Old Fen remembers every stranger since before I was born. Ironhold has archives.
Kaelen: Why are you helping me?
Elara: I haven't decided that I am.
Elara: I'm bringing a confused man with a sword somewhere with walls. That's clearing the road, not helping.
Kaelen: So I'm something in the road. I've been called worse, by people who liked me.
[if ch1_root_first_edit] Elara: And back there, you changed a Fracture directive.
[if not ch1_root_first_edit] Elara: And back there, you looked at that beast like you could read it.
do elara_looks_at_arm
Elara: That part interests me.
set ch1_personal_goal_set
do journal Personal goal: find out what happened to Flight 707. Lead: Oakhaven's road records.

# A1-P06 — First Sight of Oakhaven. No camera fly-around; the player keeps control.
~ ridge
Elara: There. Oakhaven.
Kaelen: It looks... normal. Like somewhere people live.
Elara: Rude.
Kaelen: No, I meant—
Elara: I know what you meant.
Elara: Normal's expensive lately. We work hard for it.
Kaelen: And Ironhold's that way? Past the hills?
Elara: Eventually. The road's been eating itself again.
Kaelen: Okay. Either it clears up by tomorrow, or—
Elara: —or it doesn't. Either way, you're not leaving till Bran says the road's clear. He'll want to tell you, believe me.
do objective Ask about Flight 707. Find a safe route to Ironhold.
